==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|obez|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|obez|lang=goh}}, {{term|obaz||fruit|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|Germanic|ubatjan|fruit, produce, increase|lang=de}}, from a compound whose first element represents {{proto|Indo-European|obhi-||ebhi-||bhi-|on, toward, from, by|lang=de}}, and whose second element is {{proto|Germanic|at||ēta-|edibles, food|lang=de}} from {{proto|Germanic|title=Proto-Germanic base|etanan|to eat|lang=de}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|ed-|to eat|lang=de}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|ofett||fruit, vegetable, legume|tr={{etyl|enm|-}} {{term|ovet|lang=enm}}|lang=ang}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|ovet|ōvet|lang=gml}}, {{term|avet|āvet|lang=gml}}, {{term|oft|ōft|fruit|lang=gml}}, {{etyl|dum|-}} {{term|ovet||fruit|tr={{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|ooft|lang=nl}}|lang=gml}}. More at {{l|en|ob-}}, {{l|en|eat}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|lang=de|/ʔoːpst/}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=n|gen1=Obsts|gen2=Obstes|pl=-}}

# [[fruit]]
#: ''Heute esse ich nur '''Obst'''.'' - Today I only eat fruit.

